---
title: Compute shaders
description: Dispatch GPU compute work before the base fragment render.
---

`ComputePass` runs one dispatch per rendered frame. `PingPongComputePass` repeats a compute shader over renderer-managed A/B storage-texture bindings. Both execute before the base material and do not participate in render-slot routing.

Use `PingPongShaderPass` instead when a fullscreen simulation only needs to sample the previous color texture and write the next color. Compute is appropriate for storage buffers, storage textures, explicit workgroups, and non-fragment data layouts.

## Contract

Compute source must contain:

- `@compute` and numeric `@workgroup_size(...)` dimensions;
- a function named `compute`;
- `@builtin(global_invocation_id)` in that function's parameter list.

Workgroup dimensions must be integers from 1 through 65535. The constructor and `setCompute(...)` validate the contract and extract a three-dimensional workgroup size.

## Dispatch

| Value | Resolution |
| --- | --- |
| `[x]`, `[x, y]`, `[x, y, z]` | Static workgroup counts; omitted axes become 1 |
| `'auto'` | `ceil(canvas dimension / workgroup dimension)` per axis |
| `(context) => [x, y, z]` | Dynamic counts from width, height, time, delta, and workgroup size |

Dispatch counts are validated against WebGPU limits before command encoding.

## Bindings

| Group | Generated contents |
| --- | --- |
| `0` | Frame uniforms and user uniforms |
| `1` | Storage buffers, sorted by name |
| `2` | Storage textures |

For a normal `ComputePass`, use declared resource names directly. `PingPongComputePass` generates read/write A/B bindings from its storage-texture `target` and alternates their direction across iterations.

`fragmentVisible` changes only fragment-stage sampled bindings. It does not remove the compute storage binding.

## Frame integration

All enabled compute and fragment-feedback passes retain their relative declaration order and execute before the scene. All enabled render passes retain their own relative order and execute after the scene. They share one command encoder and queue submission.

Compute pipelines are created lazily and cached. Async compilation failures are normalized as `COMPUTE_COMPILATION_FAILED` with compute-source line mapping and runtime context.

The [Particle Icosahedron demo](/playground?demo=particle-icosahedron&framework=svelte) shows storage-texture compute; the [Rubik's Cube demo](/playground?demo=rubiks-cube&framework=svelte) combines compute with storage buffers. See [Storage Buffers](/docs/storage-buffers), [Textures](/docs/textures#storage-textures), and [Passes API](/docs/api-passes-reference).
